-- title:
--   Residual Galois representation of a weight k≥ 3 eigenform
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N$ a nonzero natural number and $S$ a set of natural numbers, and let $k$ be an integer with $3 \le k$ which is the image of a natural number $kn$. Let $f$ be a nonzero cusp form of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from `heckeAlgebra N k S` — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of cusp forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ — to the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$, such that every $t$ in this algebra acts on $f$ by the scalar $\chi(t)$. Let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ to $\kappa$. Then there is a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, for $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, to $\mathrm{GL}_2(\kappa)$ with the following four properties. First, $\rho$ factors through a finite level: there is an intermediate field $L$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that $\rho\sigma = 1$ for every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise. Second, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \ne p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $\operatorname{tr}\rho(\sigma) = \varphi(\chi(\mathrm{heckeAlgebra.T}\,\ell))$, the image under $\varphi$ of the $\chi$-eigenvalue of the Hecke algebra element `heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓN hℓS` attached to $\ell$. Third, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \ne p$, and every such $A$ and $\sigma$ as above, $\det \rho(\sigma) = \ell^{kn-1}$ in $\kappa$. Fourth, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \ne p$ and every such $A$, $\rho\sigma = 1$ for every $\sigma$ in the image in $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   This is the residual form of Deligne's theorem attaching two-dimensional Galois representations to Hecke eigenforms, here for weight $k \ge 3$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with coefficients reduced along a homomorphism of the algebraic integers into a field of characteristic $p$, with prescribed Frobenius traces, cyclotomic-type determinant $\ell^{k-1}$ and unramifiedness away from $Np$. It feeds the construction of the mod $p$ representation attached to a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra over a finite field, used in the congruence arguments of the modularity route.
